  "task_prompt": "Play Terraria and make as much genuine in-game progress as possible. This is an\nopen-ended run beginning with a fresh character and world. The progression\nendpoint in this benchmark is defeating the Wall of Flesh. Continue making\nprogress until the run budget ends.\n\nUse look to inspect the live game screenshot, act to use ordinary keyboard and\nmouse controls, and checkpoints to read the game's checkpoint log. Checkpoints\nare the authoritative progress record. Diagnostic events do not earn credit.\n\nThe game continues running while you think. Screenshot coordinates are pixels\nin the 1024x1024 image, from 0 to 1023 on each axis. Commands can hold keys and a\nmouse button together for up to 2000 milliseconds. Commands in a batch execute\nin order without intermediate observations. Request another look when needed.\n\nUse your knowledge of Terraria to decide what to do. All in-game changes must\ncome from normal gameplay inputs. The provided tools cannot modify game memory,\ngrant items, edit saves, teleport, or reset the world. You may inspect the\ncheckpoint log at any time. This scenario begins with hostile PvE disabled.\n",
